REALROM sample.note c0f3 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank value is RESTORED here, not resolved: this call's helper FUN_c185 is a proven no-argument restore entry -- its own prologue reloads the bank directly from 001c, a writable RAM cell nothing between that load and the switch touches, and commits it unchanged. The bank after this call is therefore whatever was last saved at 001c, not a fresh value this analyzer failed to pin down -- a property of the game, not a gap in analysis.
